35,2,1,talk,Midori,,- **Midori**: The board minutes show the joint clinic collapsed because neither department would hold the budget line.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: The booking system only holds named clinic slots. Work without fixed appointments vanishes from every activity report.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: The therapy review shows four years of physiotherapists leaving, while midwifery has unusual slack.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: The ledger shows our allocation is down a quarter, and off-site visits draw no tariff.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: The car park fills before eleven, and the shuttle only reaches four of our nineteen villages.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,- **Midori**: That explains the joint clinic failure. We need a model where one department clearly owns the budget line.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: If the work isn’t a named slot, it’s invisible. We need a program that fits the system’s rigid structure.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,- **Misaki**: That slack in midwifery is the only breathing room I see. The therapy side is just a leak we can’t plug.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,- **Shion**: So on-site sessions are the only revenue. Home visits are a pure cost. That narrows our options sharply.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: With the car park full by eleven, any new on-site program will just add to the morning chaos.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Shion, that tariff point is critical. If home visits earn nothing, we must ensure the on-site component carries the financial weight.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, if the car park is full, how do we justify a program that requires patients to drive in?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Shion, if home visits are a pure cost, does that make the follow-up team unviable, or just expensive?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: It makes it a liability. With the allocation cut, we cannot subsidize invisible work. We need revenue.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, the shuttle gap is real, but we must prioritize the patients who can actually reach us.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,- **Midori**: Agreed. We need a program that generates revenue on-site and doesn’t rely on fragile cross-departmental agreements.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: Agreed. We need a program that fits the booking system and generates revenue, not one that vanishes from the records.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: Agreed. We need a program that uses the midwifery slack, not the therapy leak.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,Agreed. We need a program that bills on-site and fits the reduced budget. Anything else is a financial dead end.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Agreed. We need a program that fits our current capacity without overwhelming the parking or booking systems.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
