60,3,1,talk,Midori,,- **Midori**: The candidates are here. Which one fits our revenue and capacity needs?,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: The Day Rehabilitation Unit fits the booking system perfectly. Named slots, on-site billing, no hidden costs.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Misaki,,- **Misaki**: But the therapy review shows four years of physiotherapists leaving. We cannot staff a dedicated unit with a leaking team.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shion,,"- **Shion**: @Jonathan, on-site billing is good, but can we afford the fitting out? The ledger is down a quarter.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"- **Shizue**: A dedicated unit needs its own rooms. With the car park full by eleven, adding more morning traffic is impossible.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Misaki, the midwifery slack is real. The Perinatal Service uses that capacity and bills on-site.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Midori, the Perinatal Service fits the booking system and uses the midwifery slack. It avoids the therapy staffing crisis entirely.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Midori, exactly. The midwifery slack is the only stable resource we have. The Perinatal Service is the only viable option.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Midori, the Perinatal Service bills on-site, but does it require new fitting out? My ledger shows that cost is now charged against our reduced allocation.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, the Perinatal Service uses existing consultation rooms. No new fitting out is needed, so it stays within our reduced budget.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: @Shizue, that is the relief I needed. Using existing rooms means we avoid the capital trap and stay within the cut budget.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: @Shizue, that confirms it. No new fitting out means we stay within the reduced allocation. The Perinatal Service is the only logical choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"- **Misaki**: @Shizue, I agree. The midwifery slack is the only stable resource we have. The Perinatal Service is the only viable option.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Shizue, if it uses existing rooms, the capital risk is gone. I can accept the on-site billing. I’m ready to vote.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I am relieved. It fits our rooms, our parking, and our budget. I am ready to vote for the Perinatal Support Service.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Midori,,"- **Midori**: I am ready to vote for the Perinatal Support Service. It fits our budget, our staffing, and our capacity.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: I am ready to vote for the Perinatal Support Service. It fits the booking system and avoids the staffing crisis.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Misaki,,- **Misaki**: I am ready to vote for the Perinatal Support Service. It utilizes the midwifery slack and avoids the therapy staffing crisis.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shion,,"I vote for the Perinatal Support Service. It bills on-site, uses existing rooms, and fits the reduced budget.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I vote for the Perinatal Support Service. It fits our rooms, our parking, and our budget.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
